#%PAM-1.0

# timeout bounds how long a stuck fprintd session can hold the reader.
# Modules/Lock/Pam.qml mirrors the value in sessionTimeoutMs to tell an expiry
# apart from a device fault; change both together.
# Fork: max-tries=3, not 1. With 1, every miss ends the session and the shell
# forks a new PAM child + re-claims the reader (~0.5-0.8 s during which the
# sensor ignores the finger, and a finger still resting on it at re-arm reads
# as an instant smeared miss). In-session retries re-arm inside fprintd with no
# gap; Pam.qml counts each miss from the relayed error message.
auth    required    pam_fprintd.so  max-tries=3 timeout=90
account required    pam_permit.so
password required   pam_deny.so
session required    pam_permit.so
